  "interpretation": {
    "index_defect": "IntHashGrid.insert(LineString) calculates dX and dY as first minus second, then adds those differences to the first coordinate during interpolation. The reflected segment is indexed instead of the supplied segment. Native lookup near longitude 0.0299 consequently omits the containing edge94 and selects eastward edge98.",
    "index_correction": "Rebuild the derived index for the strictly verified fixture using fixed-coordinate Edge.getEnvelope() and IntHashGrid.insert(Envelope, edgeID). All street/stop/connector graph values remain identical and the original index is restored.",
    "direct_cost_before_m": 2656.089,
    "direct_cost_after_m": 2644.836,
    "independent_reference_m": 2646.439123543956,
    "reference_tolerance_m": 5.292878247087913,
    "distance_within_reference_tolerance_after_index_correction": true,
    "remaining_limit": "The envelope index correction does not repair reverse-origin costs or full-edge output geometries. Both require their separate corrections. This scoped repair is applied only after verifying existing fixture stop links; it does not correct arbitrary transit links created with the original index."
  },
